      <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      @foreach (var f in faqPairs)
      {
        <h3>@f.Q</h3>
        <p>@f.A</p>
      }

      <h2 id="related">Where to go next</h2>
      <p>This guide assumes you already know which specs you want. If you do not, <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-a-badminton-racket">how to choose a badminton racket</a> is the one to read first: it sets out the four things worth checking and where the price and benefit curve flattens.</p>
      <p>If you were hoping a racket would add power to your smash, we checked that and the answer is no: <a href="/guides/how-to-smash-harder">how to smash harder</a> covers what the measurements actually show.</p>
      <p>And the recurring cost that dwarfs the racket is shuttles. <a href="/guides/feather-vs-nylon-shuttlecocks">Feather versus nylon</a> works out what your club should be buying.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:34px;padding-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)">
        <h4 style="margin:0 0 8px">How this guide was put together</h4>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:0">ePegboard builds club-night software. We are not coaches, we do not sell rackets, and we have not tested one. We have no commercial relationship with any racket manufacturer or retailer, including the ones whose catalogues we counted, and <strong>no link on this page earns us a commission</strong>.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0">The counts come from a UK specialist's public product catalogue, captured 23 August 2026: 228 adult single rackets, after excluding 9 junior rackets and 6 multi-racket sets. Price is the lowest listed variant on the day, sale prices included, so the bands read optimistically against list price. The manufacturer figures are from Yonex UK's own public catalogue, captured 26 August 2026, 35 listings. <strong>The two captures are three days apart and we have kept their dates separate throughout</strong>, which is why the section above gives a direction rather than a percentage.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.95rem;margin:12px 0 0">Three limits worth stating. <strong>Every spec here is a retailer's or manufacturer's own marketing tag, not a measurement</strong> - and that is not our shortcut, it is the state of the category. No independent source publishes measured balance point, swingweight or shaft stiffness for retail badminton rackets, which is a striking absence next to tennis, where an equivalent public database has existed for years. <strong>The tier analysis is one brand at one retailer on one day.</strong> And the restring prices are two stringers, not a survey.</p>
        <p style="color:var(--muted-2);font-size:.9rem;margin:12px 0 0">Published 26 August 2026 by ePegboard. Catalogues captured 23 and 26 August 2026; restring prices and retailer guides read 26 August 2026.</p>
      </div>

